    "rich_text_p7D8ce": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "spacer_L8mYri": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "heading_MrGjAB": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Ivory Taper Candles FAQ",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "heading_font_class": "fs-heading-3-base"
          }
        },
        "border_JMAjFR": {
          "type": "border",
          "settings": {}
        },
        "subheading_jRWLhL": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which ivory taper height gives the most classic formal look?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_cVFhCr": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The 10\" x 0.9\" ivory tapers usually give the most classic formal look. They create enough height for a polished tablescape while still feeling balanced for dining tables, receptions, and traditional candleholders.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_ykeVbb": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fVaWkq": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are these ivory tapers a good fit for warm-toned décor?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_xVMDY7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, ivory tapers work especially well with warm-toned décor. Their softer color pairs nicely with cream linens, champagne accents, gold details, wood surfaces, and floral palettes that feel warmer and less stark than bright white.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_68L9WH": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_63Jihh": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "When should I choose 11.5-inch ivory tapers instead of 10-inch tapers?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_dttHE3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose 11.5\" ivory tapers when you want the candle to read taller and more formal from across the room. They are a stronger fit for longer holders, traditional dining setups, and tables where the candle is meant to add more height than a standard 10\" taper.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_zbiA3h": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_YnWqLz": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What is the best ivory taper for a lower-profile table?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_HcQMNY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose the 7\" x 0.8\" or 9\" x 0.8\" ivory tapers when you want the taper shape but do not want too much vertical height. Those slimmer, shorter options are easier to use on tighter tables or with fuller floral work.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_7QXgMW": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "subheading_GrTeAg": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How do I choose between 0.8-inch and 0.9-inch ivory tapers?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_ipcP9t": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose 0.9\" tapers for the fuller classic dinner-candle look and choose 0.8\" tapers when your holders run slimmer or you want a lighter line on the table. This collection gives you both widths, so the cleaner choice usually comes down to the holder and the look you are after.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_xcVwCz": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "subheading_MV8r8d": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which ivory taper pack makes the most sense for a first order?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_McHyhx": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose the 4-pack or the 10, 20, and 30-pack options if you are testing holder fit, color, or table styling before buying deeper. Those smaller counts are the easiest way to confirm the look in person before moving into the bigger case quantities.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_tzEQkU": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "subheading_DfnDnQ": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which ivory taper pack works better for a venue, restaurant, or large event?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_z9mpJd": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose the 50-pack or 100-pack when you need the same ivory taper repeated across many tables or services. The 100-pack 10\" x 0.9\" classics are especially practical when consistency matters more than buying a mix of small boxes.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_3BXfAa": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "subheading_nHwgHJ": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What makes your ivory taper assortment feel more cohesive than buying a few random taper boxes?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_RPad87": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>It gives you one Bolsius ivory taper line across the heights and pack sizes shoppers use most. That keeps the color and taper profile more consistent across the table instead of leaving you with candles that look close in a box but noticeably different once they are lit together.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_cXM7zN": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        }
      },
